::ENG2_U06_L01_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG2.C.01] A student is speaking to school leaders about after-school study space. Which opening best fits the audience?{
=A. Thank you for considering how a supervised study space could support students who remain on campus after dismissal.#Correct. This opening is respectful, clear, and audience-aware.
~B. You all need to fix this right now.#Incorrect. This is demanding and not appropriate for school leaders.
~C. The hallway is annoying and everybody knows it.#Incorrect. This is informal and vague.
~D. I just want a better place because I said so.#Incorrect. This is personal and unsupported.
}

::ENG2_U06_L01_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG2.C.01] What is the speaker's purpose if the task says, "Explain why students need a quiet place after school"?{
~A. To entertain listeners with a funny story.#Incorrect. The task asks for explanation, not entertainment.
=B. To explain a student need to listeners.#Correct. The speaker's purpose is to explain why the study space is needed.
~C. To describe every room in the school.#Incorrect. That would not match the assigned purpose.
~D. To avoid sharing a perspective.#Incorrect. Oral communication should present a clear perspective.
}

::ENG2_U06_L01_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG2.V.01] Which phrase uses the most appropriate academic vocabulary?{
~A. a cool spot#Incorrect. This is informal.
~B. a good thing#Incorrect. This is vague.
=C. a supervised academic space#Correct. This phrase is precise and appropriate for school communication.
~D. some stuff after school#Incorrect. This is vague and informal.
}

::ENG2_U06_L01_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which speaking note uses standard English conventions?{
~A. Students needs a quiet place after school.#Incorrect. Students needs should be students need.
~B. Because students wait after school.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
~C. Students wait after school, they need quiet.#Incorrect. This is a comma splice.
=D. Students who wait after school need a quiet place to complete assignments.#Correct. This is complete, clear, and correctly written.
}

::ENG2_U06_L01_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG2.R.10] Passage idea: A strong student speaker explains purpose, considers audience, and presents a respectful perspective. Which summary is most accurate?{
~A. Student speakers should only say what they want.#Incorrect. The passage says speakers should explain more than what they want.
=B. Student speakers should shape their message around purpose, audience, and perspective.#Correct. This accurately summarizes the passage.
~C. Student speakers should avoid respectful language.#Incorrect. The passage specifically values respect.
~D. Student speakers should read every sentence from a script.#Incorrect. The passage does not say this.
}
